show-websocket-retry-on-first-failure

Lane: mixed

Unit: recover-websocket-requests-without-http-fallback

ChildPatch: show-websocket-retry-on-first-failure

Form: GitDiff

Segment: snapshot

Purpose: Keep official personal ChatGPT WebSocket recovery visible and persistent without silently switching to HTTP.

Requires: none

Provides: For Plus, Pro and ProLite on the unmodified official endpoint, show the first retry and retain WebSocket transport; with the default five-retry budget, sampling capacity failures wait for the next five-minute boundary and exhausted connection failures restart their cycle there until cancellation, with visible TUI warning records.

Boundary: Other plans, API keys, endpoint overrides, custom budgets and remote compaction retain native retry timing. Atomic response admission, response-progress deadline integration, usage observations, hard cancellation and input preemption retain their own responsibilities; this recovery feature does not require response collection.

Verification: Client account and fallback tests, response-retry clock and cancellation tests, and TUI overload-warning tests verify eligibility, strict boundary timing, cycle reset, compaction exclusion, and one visible diagnostic with native retry status.


